    // Optimized schedules.
    //
    // Goals:
    //  - Exploit data locality in A, r, p.
    //  - Vectorize inner loops along contiguous memory dimensions.
    //  - Parallelize across independent output elements (s[j], q[i]).
    //
    // Memory layout:
    //   Buffer A(m, n) has dimension 0 (j) contiguous and dimension 1 (i) strided.
    //   A_param(j, i) is therefore laid out with j contiguous.
    //
    // For q(i):
    //   q(i) += sum_j A_param(j, i) * p(j)
    //   At fixed i, varying j reads A_param(j, i) contiguously in j (dim 0).
    //   We keep j (rj) as inner loop and vectorize over rj.
    //
    // For s(j):
    //   s(j) += sum_i r(i) * A_param(j, i)
    //   At fixed i, varying j reads A_param(j, i) contiguously in j (dim 0).
    //   We therefore iterate outer over i (ri) and inner over j, and
    //   vectorize over j.
